  "body": "## Summary\n\n- expose OpenMediaVault mounted file systems through the existing storage volume selector\n- enable scoped volume filtering for OpenMediaVault and mixed OpenMediaVault/Synology widget configurations\n- add regression coverage and update widget/integration documentation\n\nCloses #6626\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/integrations/src/openmediavault/test/openmediavault-integration.spec.ts packages/widgets/src/filter-storage-volumes.spec.ts --coverage.enabled=false` (21 tests passed)\n- `pnpm typecheck` (37 tasks passed)\n- `pnpm turbo lint --filter=@homarr/integrations --filter=@homarr/api --filter=@homarr/widgets --filter=@homarr/translation --filter=@homarr/docs` (no errors)\n- `pnpm turbo build --filter=@homarr/docs`\n- Next.js production build via `pnpm --filter @homarr/nextjs run with-env next build` with `CI` and `HOMARR_VERSION` set explicitly\n- changed-file `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check`\n\n## Local validation notes\n\nThe root `pnpm build` wrapper reaches the Next.js task but its POSIX `HOMARR_VERSION=$(...)` assignment cannot be parsed by Windows `cmd.exe`. Running the equivalent Next.js production build with the environment set explicitly succeeds. The repository-wide formatter reports pre-existing drift outside this patch; every changed file passes the formatter directly.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Builds without warnings or errors (`pnpm build`, autofix with `pnpm format:fix`)\n- [x] Pull request targets `dev` branch\n- [x] Commits follow the conventional commits guideline\n- [x] No shorthand variable names are used\n- [x] Documentation is up to date\n- [x] No temporary files are checked in and the code follows the existing project style\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added OpenMediaVault support for listing and filtering visible storage volumes.\n  - Storage-volume selection is now available when all selected integrations are OpenMediaVault or Synology.\n  - Added OpenMediaVault storage volumes to the System Disks and Health Monitoring widgets.\n  - The filter is hidden when unsupported integrations are included.\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Updated integration and widget documentation to describe supported configurations and filtering behavior.\n\n- **Tests**\n  - Added coverage for OpenMediaVault volume discovery, filtering, and supported integration combinations.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
